=== PARITY (vs web ChargeSessionChartWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (ChargeSessionChartSource -> ChargeSessionChartModel):
    useVehicles, useQuery(GET /charging?vehicle_id&limit=10), useDateFormat, useTranslation. The production app
    wires ChargeSessionChartSource over the KMP ChargingStore (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>>) with the
    user Settings supplying locale/timezone; the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection -> ChargeSessionBuilder is a 1:1 port of the web useMemo pipeline:
    classifyChargerType (charger_type contains supercharger|tesla -> supercharger; non-empty, non-'<invalid>'
    -> dc; else home), convertEnergyFromSI(total_energy_added_wh ?? 0, 'kWh') = Wh/1000, label =
    formatDateShort(started_at) || '#i+1', .reverse() so the oldest session is leftmost, Total/Avg energy +
    session count, hasData = chartData.length > 0 (a 0-kWh session still counts — distinct from MonthlyMileage).
    Verified by executed XCTest on iOS Simulator AND macOS.
  Composition -> widget shell chrome (bolt icon in emerald + "Charge Sessions" title + freshness chip + refresh
    + optional open) · 3-stat header (Total / Avg with kWh unit · Sessions count) · bar chart (one bar per
    session, colored by charger bucket, tap-to-inspect tooltip showing date + energy + charger type, persistent
    home/Supercharger/DC legend under the chart) · compact (cols<=1 && rows<=1) shows stats only, standard shows
    stats+chart, wide (cols>=3) thins the x-axis date labels — all web branches.
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion / TSSkeleton (compiled
    against the REAL apps/apple component library + KMP framework in the Xcode build below).
    Recharts BarChart/Bar/Cell/Tooltip/XAxis/YAxis -> SwiftUI Charts BarMark + chartXSelection annotation +
    token-styled chartXAxis/chartYAxis. CHARGER_COLORS hex map -> design-token status palette EXACTLY:
    supercharger #ef4444 = statusDanger, dc #f59e0b = statusWarning, home #10b981 = statusSuccess. Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No charge sessions yet" ContentUnavailableView) ·
    error (retry) · stale (chip + banner + 30s auto-refresh) · offline (cached value + chip + banner) · content.
    Model phase resolution keeps cached bars visible behind refresh/offline/error (web shell).
  i18n -> all 9 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.chargeSessionChart.title, .total, .avg, .sessions, .empty, .type.home, .type.supercharger, .type.dc,
